														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2803265">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>I'm talking like… handcuffs with a syringe.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Think of it as a sculpture utilizing a nontraditional medium. The title of the piece, the associated cognitohazard, it's all the artist trying to say something.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Item is a pair of handcuffs of the same model as those issued to the ██████, ██ Police Department from ████ to ████ and a hypodermic needle within a plexiglass display case.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The two items are together to indicate that they're really the same thing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>When directly observed by a human being, the handcuffs appear unlocked and the needle appears to be capped and sealed in a sterilized pouch, but when recorded with digital and film photography, the handcuffs appear locked and the needle appears to be broken.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Human sight can be fallible, can be subjective. A camera, unless tampered with, cannot. So the handcuffs only look unlocked, the needle only looks clean. They're not.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A plaque is fixed to the display case that reads: &quot;Chains.&quot; This is presumably the title of the piece.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The artist is playing with perception again. She's saying that the drugs and the system in place for dealing with addiction are really the same thing and that thing is shackles, holding people like her brother back.</p>
<p>As I said, think of it as a sculpture. Instead of clay and marble, the artist just used extant objects. Instead of angle tricks, she used some sort of magic to make it look different depending on how it's viewed.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Tl;dr: Are We Cool Yet?</p>

