<p>I might be interested in seeing some more, listed on another page (sort of a 'Link to full catalog of objects found within SCP-2739)</p>
<p>As far as the PoI logs, at least where the idea of PoI has developed, I think the artist doesn't need a full log, while the subject of the art wouldn't really count as a PoI as I understand it, but at least for now, the summary of their life is helpful to have (Perhaps list them as 'the former occupant of SCP-2739,')</p>
<p>I really like how you tell a story without relying on excess narrative. My biggest annoyance since I started browsing the wiki again has been the excessive reliance on spelling things out for me, since much of the (for lack of a better word) fun for me is in putting things together. And all the art in here really works well. A worse author would have burdened it with interviews with the PoI and maybe even one of the artworks displaying some level of intelligence. By just telling us what the person is and what the art shows, we can feel it stronger than if we had a long interview. This is one of my favorite SCPs yet.</p>

